      "leadImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Cove_Harbour_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled",
      "source": "Wikipedia"
    },
    "town": {
      "title": "Cockburnspath",
      "description": "Village in the Scottish Borders",
      "extract": "Cockburnspath is a village in Berwickshire in the Scottish Borders. It lies near the North Sea coast between Berwick-upon-Tweed and Dunbar. Cockburnspath is the eastern terminus of the Southern Upland Way as well as the northern terminus of the Berwickshire Coastal Path. At the nearby village of Cove, there is a small fishing harbour.",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockburnspath",
      "coordinates": {
